WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.600
Why is a square root called a square root?

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.020
Why does it have the word square in it?

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.040
Also, why does a number to the power of two get called a square?

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.960
I'll explain, but pause the video if you want to try figuring it out yourself first.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.160
Okay, here's the answer.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.180
If you square a number you basically multiply it by itself,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.860
so for example four squared is four timesfour, which equals 16.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:31.600
Now if you draw this on a graph and put the first four on the horizontal axis and the second four on the vertical axis,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.000
You actually get a square which has got an area 16 because it's four times four.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.860
So that's where the word square comes from in

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.340
squared and square root.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.860
Basically when you do a square root of a number let's say 20,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:52.280
You're saying, if I have a square with the area of 20, what's the length of one of the sides? In this case

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.800
In this case, it's 4.47 blah blah blah...

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.300
Now some numbers are called perfect squares, which means when you square root them the answer is a whole number.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.580
So the square root of 16 is 4, so 16 is a perfect square.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:16.760
If the number isn't a perfect square like 20, then the square root is a decimal like 4.472

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.620
Blah-Blah-Blah-Blah-Blah, so 20 isn't a perfect square.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.200
Here's another interesting thing,

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:27.800
the answer to square root is always a little imprecise, because there are actually two answers.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:33.880
A positive and a negative one, so the square root of 16 is actually both plus 4 and minus 4.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:43.520
This is because - 4 Squared also gives you 16 because it's -4 x -4 and a negative number times a negative number equals a positive number.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.600
So you don't know which one it is so people normally just take the positive

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.580
and this is interesting because it's also why you can never have the square root of a negative number.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
This is because nothing times itself makes a negative number

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.420
It's also like having a square with a negative area

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:06.840
which you can in fact get if you look at our graph it would come from 4 x -4

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.320
or -4 x 4 but -4 and 4 are different numbers

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.680
so it can't be the answer to a square root

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:21.760
and beyond that when you've got a number to the power of three it's called a cube,  because you multiply it by itself three times

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.160
extending it out into the third dimension

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.380
and the opposite of this is called the cube root.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.460
Then also if you've got a number to the power of four you extend it out into the fourth dimension,

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:41.440
but this is totally hard to draw or even imagine so you kind of just have to trust the maths.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.420
So this is why it's called the square root.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:55.320
I also looked up where the word root comes from in Square root and the root of that word is from the Roman word

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.540
Radix which is also. Why the symbol for square root is called a radical.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.800
Who knew?

